where do i had my index file here

You’re currently on the empty root page of the repo, so you haven’t uploaded anything yet.

Click this link on the page:

uploading an existing file

or directly go here:

Upload files to jamesriverhome

Then:

Drag your index.html file into the upload area
Also drag:
any CSS files
JS files
images
video assets
folders like assets, images, etc.
Scroll down

Click:

Commit changes

After upload:

go to Settings
then Pages

under “Branch” choose:

main
/(root)
click Save

Then GitHub Pages will generate your live site URL in about 30–90 seconds.

Your site will end up at something like:

https://robbjprice.github.io/jamesriverhome/

Classic GitHub moment by the way:
“Here’s an empty repo. Good luck, astronaut.”

i just need to paste html code

You haven’t turned on GitHub Pages yet. Right now you only uploaded the file into the repo.

Do this:

Click the Settings tab at the top of the repo page
In the LEFT sidebar, click:
Pages
Under:
Build and deployment

set:

Source → Deploy from a branch
Branch → main
Folder → / (root)
Click Save

Then wait about 30–60 seconds.

Then your preview/site will load here:

Preview the James River Retreat website

Right now if you open it immediately, you may get:

404
blank page
or “site not found”

That’s normal until GitHub finishes deploying.

Also important:
Your site WILL initially show missing images because your HTML references files like:

images/hero-exterior.jpg
images/living-room.jpg

…but those images are not uploaded yet.

So after the site loads:

create an images folder in the repo
upload your house photos there
rename them to match the filenames in the HTML

The structure is already built correctly. The preview issue is just GitHub Pages not enabled yet.

